LICENSING FOR THE FILES IN THIS DIRECTORY
=========================================

The MIT licence in the repository root covers the CODE only. It does NOT cover
the datasets below, which are redistributed from third-party sources and keep
their original terms.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SEntFiN-v1.1.csv
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source : SEntFiN 1.0 — Entity-aware sentiment analysis for financial news
Authors: Ankur Sinha, Satishwar Kedas, Rishu Kumar, Pekka Malo (2022)
         Journal of the Association for Information Science and Technology

Redistributed here for reproducibility. If you use this data, cite the authors.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
phrasebank_and_sentfin.csv
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
A DERIVED WORK combining SEntFiN 1.1 with the Financial PhraseBank.

Financial PhraseBank
  Source : Good debt or bad debt: Detecting semantic orientations in
           economic texts
  Authors: Pekka Malo, Ankur Sinha, Pekka Korhonen, Jyrki Wallenius,
           Petri Takala (2014), Journal of the Association for Information
           Science and Technology
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/

Because Financial PhraseBank is CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, this derived file is
distributed under the SAME LICENCE:

    phrasebank_and_sentfin.csv is licensed CC BY-NC-SA 3.0

That means, if you reuse it, you must:
  * ATTRIBUTE the original authors (both papers above);
  * use it for NON-COMMERCIAL purposes only;
  * distribute any derivative of it under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 as well.

The Financial PhraseBank half is not redistributed in raw form anywhere else
in this repository — the notebook loads it at runtime from the HuggingFace
`financial_phrasebank` dataset (configuration `sentences_50agree`).
